meta {
  name: Projects
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/method/implementor.client_api.get_projects
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  ~kind: implementation
  ~customer: Hamza
}

tests {
  test("returns 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("message is an array", function () {
    expect(res.body.message).to.be.an("array");
  });

  test("each item has a kind", function () {
    res.body.message.forEach(function (p) {
      expect(p.kind).to.be.oneOf(["implementation", "amc"]);
    });
  });
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  The client's projects, implementation and AMC, as summary cards.

  **Endpoint:** `GET /api/method/implementor.client_api.get_projects`
  **Screen:** Projects list (Services uses the same items, grouped)

  **Permission:** Signed-in client user (Client User or Client Admin). Only records of the user's own client company are returned.

  **Query parameters:**

  | Field | Type | Required | Example | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `kind` | string | no | `implementation` | `implementation` or `amc`. Leave it out (or empty) for all. Any other value also returns all. |
  | `customer` | string | no | `Hamza` | Not used by the app. The server picks the user's company. Disabled by default. |

  **Response:** a list, most recently changed project first. Cancelled and closed projects are left out.

  ```json
  {
    "message": [
      {
        "name": "PROJ-0029",
        "title": "ERPNext Implementation - Hamza Trading",
        "display_title": "ERPNext Implementation",
        "kind": "implementation",
        "status": "active",
        "start_date": "2026-08-01",
        "end_date": "2026-12-31",
        "days_left": 55,
        "project_manager": "Sahana",
        "stage": "Data Migration",
        "phase": { "index": 3, "count": 8, "name": "Data Migration" },
        "health": "green",
        "percent": 62,
        "go_live_date": "2026-12-15",
        "go_live_days_left": 39,
        "next_milestone": { "title": "Configuration complete", "end_date": "2026-11-20", "days_left": 14, "status": "in_progress" }
      },
      {
        "name": "PROJ-0030",
        "title": "AMC - Hamza Trading",
        "display_title": "AMC",
        "kind": "amc",
        "status": "amc",
        "start_date": "2026-01-01",
        "end_date": "2026-12-31",
        "days_left": 55,
        "project_manager": "Sahana",
        "contract_status": "active",
        "elapsed_percent": 85,
        "hours_used": 18.5,
        "hours_included": 40,
        "tickets": { "open": 2, "closed": 9 }
      }
    ]
  }
  ```

  **Fields on every item:**

  - `name`: send this as `project` to Implementation, AMC or Milestones.
  - `display_title`: show this, not `title` (the customer name suffix is removed).
  - `kind`: `implementation` or `amc`. Decides which fields follow and which screen to open.
  - `status`: project status code: `discovery`, `active`, `go_live`, `amc`, `hypercare` or `closed`.
  - `end_date`: expected end date, or the deadline when no end date is set. `days_left`: days until it, negative when past, null without an end date.
  - `project_manager`: full name. Can be null.

  **Implementation items only:**

  - `stage`: stage label as stored: `Discovery`, `Config`, `Data Migration`, `Integration`, `UAT`, `Training`, `Go-Live` or `Hypercare`.
  - `phase`: `index` (1-based), `count` and `name`. Null when the stage isn't one of the known phases.
  - `health`: `green`, `amber` or `red`. Null when not set.
  - `percent`: overall progress, 0 to 100.
  - `go_live_date`, `go_live_days_left`: go-live date (falls back to the deadline) and days until it; negative means overdue.
  - `next_milestone`: first milestone of the project's contract type (see Milestones) still open or awaiting sign-off: `title`, `end_date`, `days_left` and `status` (`not_started`, `in_progress`, `partially_completed`, `on_hold`, `due` or `completed`). Null when none.

  **AMC items only:**

  - `contract_status`: `active`, `expiring` (30 days or less left) or `expired`. Null without an end date.
  - `elapsed_percent`: how much of the contract period has passed, 0 to 100. Null without a start or end date.
  - `hours_used`: hours logged on the contract's tasks. `hours_included`: contracted hours, null when not set.
  - `tickets`: `open` and `closed` counts for the contract.

  **Errors:** client API errors have an `error_code`; auth errors raised by Frappe don't.

  - **401** (no error_code): token expired or invalid. Refresh once and retry, else sign out.
  - **403** (no error_code): no Authorization header sent.
  - **403** `no_client_linked`: the user isn't linked to any client company.

  **Notes:**

  - Implementation, AMC and Milestones still open a closed or cancelled project by its `name`; only this list leaves them out.
  - Empty list: show "No projects yet".
}
